        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">b continuant part of c at all times =Def for all times t, (b exists at t, implies b continuant part of c at t &amp; t is a temporal region &amp; b and c are continuants)</skos:definition>
        <skos:example xml:lang="en">Centre of mass of a material entity continuant part of material entity at all times; continuant fiat external boundary of an object continuant part of object at all times.</skos:example>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">continuant part of at all times</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


